Here's TUnit's lifecycle at each scope:

## 1. Before/After Every Test in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Test)]
    public async Task ResetDatabase(TestContext context)
    {
        await InMemoryDb.ResetAsync();
    }

    [After(Test)]
    public async Task Cleanup(TestContext context)
    {
        // optional per-test teardown
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task Order_WithNoItems_Throws() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 2. Once Before/After All Tests in a Class

```csharp
public class OrderTests
{
    [Before(Class)]
    public static async Task OpenFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once before the first test in this class
    }

    [After(Class)]
    public static async Task DisposeFixture(ClassHookContext context)
    {
        // runs once after the last test in this class
    }

    [Test]
    public async Task PlaceOrder_Succeeds() { /* ... */ }
}
```

## 3. Once Before/After All Tests in the Assembly

```csharp
public class WireMockHook
{
    [Before(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StartWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // starts once before any test in this assembly
    }

    [After(Assembly)]
    public static async Task StopWireMock(AssemblyHookContext context)
    {
        // stops once after all tests in this assembly finish
    }
}
```

## 4. Once for the Entire Test Session (cross-assembly)

```csharp
public class GlobalDatabaseHook
{
    [Before(TestSession)]
    public static async Task ApplyMigrations(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // runs once at the very start of the test run
    }

    [After(TestSession)]
    public static async Task TearDownDatabase(TestSessionContext context)
    {
        // runs once at the very end of the test run
    }
}
```

---

**Key points:**

| Scope | Attribute | Method must be |
|-------|-----------|----------------|
| Per-test | `[Before(Test)]` / `[After(Test)]` | Instance |
| Per-class | `[Before(Class)]` / `[After(Class)]` | `static` |
| Per-assembly | `[Before(Assembly)]` / `[After(Assembly)]` | `static` |
| Per-session | `[Before(TestSession)]` / `[After(TestSession)]` | `static` |

All hooks can be `async Task` and optionally accept a `CancellationToken` as a second parameter.

**Bonus:** Use `[BeforeEvery(Test)]` / `[AfterEvery(Test)]` (static, in any class) for a *global* cross-cutting hook that fires for every test in the run regardless of class.
